      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. It verifies that parsing with `stopAtNonOption=true` returns a non-null `CommandLine` even when an unrecognized option token is encountered. Let me write the improved version.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version improves understandability by using descriptive variable names (`emptyOptions`, `parser`, `args`, `result`), removing unused imports (`Properties`, `Consumer`), and adding a Javadoc comment plus inline comment that explain the intent — that `stopAtNonOption=true` causes graceful stopping rather than an exception when an unrecognized token is encountered."
